    "body": "fix on issue/1865-dxf-insert · PR #4052 · pinned by blocks::insert_moves_turns_and_scales_a_block_keeping_arcs_exact, blocks::a_mirrored_insert_reverses_the_arc, blocks::unequal_scale_turns_a_circle_into_tangent_arcs_within_the_bound, blocks::nested_blocks_compose_and_layer_zero_takes_the_insert_layer, block_refusals::cyclic_missing_and_too_deep_blocks_are_refused_by_name, block_refusals::copy_counts_past_the_vertex_limit_are_refused_without_the_work, arcs::an_inserted_block_cuts_and_posts_like_the_same_top_level_circle · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR expands each INSERT of a BLOCK: move, turn, scale, mirror, row and column arrays, and nested blocks up to 8 levels. Arcs stay exact under an equal scale. An unequal scale gives tangent arcs within 1 µm. Block geometry on layer 0 takes the layer of its INSERT. Cycles, missing blocks, deep nesting and too many copies are refused by name. This is the last open part of this issue, so the PR uses `Fixes #1865`.",
